{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'FM_HOME|export|setup|environment' docs/arm-pretool-check.md\"","aggregated_output":"7:`bin/fm-arm-command-policy.mjs` is also the sole owner of firstmate's shell classification: it exports the tokenizer and command-position analysis, which the sibling cd-guard seatbelt (`bin/fm-cd-pretool-check.sh`, `docs/cd-guard.md`) reuses instead of duplicating shell lexing.\n32:The active firstmate home is `${FM_HOME:-<code-root>}`.\n70:Suffix matching recognizes an expanded-path prefix statically, so `$FM_HOME/bin/fm-watch-arm.sh`, `$HOME/firstmate/bin/fm-watch-arm.sh`, and `~/firstmate/bin/fm-watch-arm.sh` are the arm identity.\n95:An allowed watcher program is one linear outer command list with zero or more approved setup nodes followed by exactly one direct protected node.\n98:Approved setup nodes are:\n101:- `export NAME=<one shell word>` with no command substitution, process substitution, or redirection.\n106:An absolute x-mode path outside the active home is not an approved setup node.\n109:`&&` is accepted after setup so a failed `cd`, `export`, or source prevents the protected call from running under the wrong setup.\n115:Inline environment assignments, `env`, `sudo`, `nohup`, nested shells, `eval`, subshell groups, substitutions, redirections, pipelines, asynchronous lists, `disown`, unrelated list nodes, and unsupported compound syntax are not blessed.\n140:| `watcher-bundled` | The outer command list is not the blessed setup-plus-final tree. |\n175:Cursor also loads `<project>/.claude/settings.json`, so the tracked Claude entry receives the same event. Without `--cursor` a Cursor-delivered payload is that duplicate and allows without re-classifying, decided from the payload's own `cursor_version` by `bin/fm-hook-host-lib.sh`; [`turnend-guard.md`](turnend-guard.md#harness-integrations) owns why that predicate reads the payload rather than the environment.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
